// Oracle batch 200 (levels/pokitaru-hoven, release 0.3.0): level 12's (Hoven) own code on its real level data. Run with
// ORACLE_LEVEL=12 build/tests/ovl_oracle --batch 200 (needs the ISO; no RAM dumps). The subjects are the level's own mobys of each class
// (placed by its gameplay data) after the first gameplay frame, perturbed; the original is level 12's own function at its own address, the
// port the one registered for it (the transliterations hoven_classes_tr_N.cpp, generated by tools/codegen/mkall_l12.py, group
// hoven_classes):
//  - the 51 class updates of the level's own code (class table, overlay section 3 at 0x20cb80);
//  - the eleven draw-list callbacks the classes queue (19, 293, 384, 832, 1135, 1267's two, 1345, 1818, 1901, a helper's);
//  - sound emitter types 1 / 3 / 5 / 6 (section 5 at 0x20d380) on the level's emitters;
//  - class 238's five hooks (table 0x20d228; +0x10 is paired by the overlay map with Veldin's 0x2d5800, whose record offset differs)
//    and class 270's hook +0xc (table 0x20d240: Veldin's 0x2caf10 code, paired by the map with 0x2d57d0);
//  - camera type 0x12's accept (L12:0x316478; its init / update / exit are Veldin's), the camera mode hook (0x3148f0) and the callback
//    it queues (0x314950);
//  - the movement-mode hero update (L12:0x2290e8, the Novalis family's 0x3a8-byte build, hoven_hero_tr_1.cpp);
//  - moby_spawn and mobys_in_sphere (the Veldin ports) against level 12's own copies.
// The hero controller (hoven_hero_tr_N.cpp, the variants of variants_l12.cpp) is proved by the hero batches 44..55 with ORACLE_LEVEL=12.

